# /etc/default/weftd — optional environment for the weftd log agent.
#
# weftd is configured by the YAML file you author at
# /etc/weftd/config.yaml (start from /etc/weftd/config.yaml.example).
# That file is the single source of truth for endpoint, sources, kinds,
# metavariables, metrics — everything. This package never generates or
# overwrites it.
#
# The ONLY thing this file is for is the auth token, as a credential
# chain: if WEFTD_TOKEN is set here it overrides the `token:` in the
# config file (AWS-shaped — env wins, file is the fallback). Use this
# when a secret injector / config management supplies the token out of
# band and you don't want it written into the YAML. If you put the
# token in config.yaml, leave this unset and you can ignore this file.
#
# Nothing structural belongs here — there are deliberately no
# WEFTD_APP / WEFTD_LOG_PATH / WEFTD_* knobs anymore; author the YAML.
#
# NOTE: the WEFTD_ prefix is intentional. Hosts that also run the weft
# coordinator use unprefixed admin vars (DB_DSN, SHARD_ASG_SMALL, …);
# keeping the agent token under WEFTD_ avoids collisions.

# Agent auth token issued by weft. Overrides `token:` in
# /etc/weftd/config.yaml when set. Leave unset to use the file's token.
#WEFTD_TOKEN=
